  "content": "Week 50: Rapid Miner\n\nThis week I was majorly doing data mining homework. I have to say, I have never used rapid miner before. I think this is a good tool compare to python. You can focus more on the data not the code.\n\nIt is meanly linear regression, decision tree. We use ANN, KNN to do classification. Calculate correlation. Association rules. They are very useful when you collect a mount of values.\n\nMovies and TVs\n\nThe Substance, not a good movie to watch when you are eating. However, I mean the professionals are really good at catching the best part of female body. It is good to watch but don't in the food time.\n\nWhat if the last season has started. The first episode is not so fun to watch. But consider Agatha all along is unexpectedly good. I am looking forward to that.",
